# Testing Patterns

**Status: Vitest is planned but not installed yet.** There is no test
runner or test file in this repo today. This file describes the intended
patterns for when tests are added — don't reference `jest`, `jest.mock`,
or `jest-environment-jsdom` in new code or docs.

## Test Structure

- Use descriptive test names: `it("rejects a file over 5 MB before reading it")`, not `it("works")`.
- Organize with `describe` blocks that mirror the module under test.
- Follow Arrange-Act-Assert (AAA) in every test.
- Use `beforeEach`/`afterEach` for setup and teardown; clean up any side effects.

## Mapping tests to acceptance criteria

- Every new test must trace to a specific, approved acceptance criterion
  in `FDO-action-dispatch/ACTION_DISPATCH_ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA.md` — don't
  write speculative tests for behavior that isn't specified there.
- Always test the happy path, at least one error/rejection case, and the
  empty/no-data case for any new user-facing behavior.

## React / component testing (once needed)

- Use `@testing-library/react`. Prefer `screen.getByRole` /
  `screen.getByLabelText` over `getByTestId`.
- Test user-visible behavior (what the operator sees/can do), not
  internal implementation details.

## Mocking

- Mock external dependencies (the Zapier SDK, AI-by-Zapier calls) at the
  boundary. Never mock the module under test.
- Prefer `vi.spyOn` over `vi.mock` when only one method needs overriding.
- Reset mocks in `afterEach`: `vi.restoreAllMocks()`.

## Security- and privacy-relevant tests

- Test that oversized/unsupported/malformed/empty input is rejected
  *before* any content is read, parsed, or acted on.
- Test that a rejected or cancelled operation leaves existing state
  (e.g. transcript editor content) unchanged.
- Test that error messages shown to the user never contain raw
  exceptions, stack traces, or file-path internals.
